I think it largely depends on my pet.  Depending on my starting spells, I'll
either get a couple of levels (for more pw) ot try out being a pacifist for
a while.  My goal as an early wizard is to keep my XP low, and my pet alive.
If the pet is doing all the killing, then it will grow fairly quickly and
become quite tough.  My next goal is to find a coaligned or unattended
altar, and sacrifice for Magicbane.  Once I have that, the game gets quite a
bit easier, as most enemies in the early game rely on hand to hand attacks,
and magicbane can completely prevent those.  Also, wearing certain types of
armor isn't so bad, you can usually get away with wearing a metal helm and
boots and the failure rates won't be too bad.  Next goal is to get to XP 14
and learn a useful attack spell (fireball or cone of cold) and get attack
spells up to skilled at least.  The quest is a breeze if you've got the
right spells, and once you have the eye, pretty much nothing can stop you.

Generally, I would suggest doing the mines down to minetown, and then doing
sokobon, before returning and finishing the mines.  You've got a 1/3 chance
of  the minetown altar being coaligned, and getting magicbane early on can
be helpful, also, sometimes magic lamps are for sale in the shops...


